Working state|git status --short --branch|Summarizes branch and file changes.|Check for local work before switching or rewriting history.|The two status columns describe index and working-tree changes; ?? means untracked.|## feature...origin/feature ; M app.js|Read-only; does not show ignored files by default.
Unstaged diff|git diff|Compares working-tree content with the index.|Review edits not yet staged.|Minus lines are removed and plus lines added relative to the index; staged-only changes are absent.|diff --git a/app.js b/app.js|Read-only; output may contain secrets introduced locally.
Staged diff|git diff --staged|Compares the index with HEAD.|Review exactly what a normal commit would include.|Only staged changes appear; later unstaged edits may differ.|--- a/file ; +++ b/file|Read-only; inspect before committing.
Whitespace validation|git diff --check|Checks the selected diff for whitespace errors and conflict-marker problems.|Catch accidental formatting damage before review.|Output names files and lines with issues; no output usually means no detected issue.|file:12: trailing whitespace|Read-only; this is not a syntax or semantic test.
Fetch remote state|git fetch origin|Downloads objects and updates origin remote-tracking references.|Inspect upstream changes without integrating them into the current branch.|Updated reference ranges show what changed; the working tree stays unchanged.|abc123..def456 main -> origin/main|Changes local remote-tracking refs and contacts the remote; does not merge.
History graph|git log --graph --oneline --decorate -20|Shows a compact recent commit graph with reference names.|Understand branching, merges and the current base.|Stars are commits; connecting lines show parent relationships; labels identify refs.|* abc123 (HEAD -> feature) Fix validation|Read-only; the graph is limited to the selected history and count.
Commit details|git show --stat HEAD|Displays the current commit summary and file-change statistics.|Review the scope of the latest commit.|The stat counts changed lines by file; use a full diff for actual content.|3 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)|Read-only; statistics do not establish correctness.
Branch tracking|git branch -vv|Lists local branches with tips and upstream information.|Find a branch tracking the wrong remote or lacking an upstream.|Brackets show upstream and ahead/behind relative to last fetched state.|* main abc123 [origin/main] ...|Read-only; fetch first when current remote state matters.
Ignore diagnosis|git check-ignore -v PATH|Explains which ignore pattern matches a path.|Find why a generated or source file does not appear as expected.|Output identifies rule file, line number and pattern.|.gitignore:12:dist/ dist/app.js|Read-only; replace PATH and remember tracked files are not untracked ignore candidates.
Local recovery history|git reflog --date=iso -10|Shows recent local reference movements.|Locate a commit lost after reset or rebase.|Each entry includes a reachable historical tip and the operation that moved it.|HEAD@{...}: rebase (finish): ...|Read-only; entries expire and do not guarantee recovery of uncommitted changes.
Changed filenames|git diff --name-status origin/main...HEAD|Lists changes introduced since the merge base with origin/main.|Review branch scope relative to its base.|A, M and D indicate added, modified and deleted paths; three dots use the merge base.|M app.js|Read-only; ensure origin/main is freshly fetched and is the intended comparison branch.
Release tags|git tag --list 'v*' --sort=-version:refname|Lists version-like tags in version-aware descending order.|Inspect available release references.|Names are tags, not proof that an artifact exists or was verified.|v2.1.0 ; v2.0.0|Read-only; verify tag identity and release artifact separately.
